⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⣴⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿⣇


A Just-In-Time compiler for the Exo language.


Exo's default backend emits C, requiring an offline
compile step. exojit lowers Exo IR through xDSL to
LLVM and compiles it at import time via llvmlite MCJIT.

Tensors and externally supplied windows use contiguous row-major storage
and a bare-pointer ABI. MLIR/JIT normalizes ordinary calls and local windows
using Exo's inline/inline_window APIs, composing source indices for rows,
columns and chained views. No shape/stride descriptor or hidden stride
arguments are passed, including for standalone callees.

to_mlir still returns an xDSL ModuleOp and emits the full original
ordinary-procedure closure as exports. Original precision, window and
memory checks run before call boundaries disappear. The Python-list and
raw-pointer JIT interfaces are unchanged. Source-declared dimensions,
not loop bounds, determine addressing after inlining.

Instruction calls retain the native-symbol ABI: provide a symbol named
after the instruction procedure, with scalar values and bare buffer
pointers (view origins for windows). Specifications are never inlined;
arbitrary C templates are not implemented by MLIR/JIT. Standalone
instructions remain skipped as exports; --c still uses Exo's C backend.

There is no fixed expansion cap; inlining increases compile time and IR
size. Normalization is BLOCKED for a local window preceding 1200 unrolled
assignments: pinned Exo inline_window raises RecursionError, although the
non-normalizing compiler accepts this input. General externally supplied
strided windows remain unsupported.


    $ uv run exojit example.py --mlir
    $ uv run exojit example.py --c
    $ uv run example.py


I also reimplemented microGPT with every kernel written
in Exo and benchmarked it against NumPy, PyTorch, JAX,
and karpathy's original scalar autograd.


     name      mean μs  ±σ     min    max     speedup 
    ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
     exojit    35       0      35     35      1902    
     numpy     176      133    140    3011    378     
     torch     185      25     165    391     360     
     jax       503      0      503    503     132     
     plain     7042     720    6670   18530   9       
     original  66601    20604  20522  179583  1       


